1
00:00:00,107 --> 00:00:04,567
(Leonard:)Now that I'm actually about to go out
with Penny, I'm not excited, I'm nauseous.

2
00:00:04,737 --> 00:00:06,527
(Sheldon:)Then your meal choice is appropriate.

3
00:00:06,697 --> 00:00:07,777
(Sheldon:)Starch absorbs fluid...

4
00:00:07,948 --> 00:00:11,578
(Sheldon:)...which reduces the amount
of vomit available for violent expulsion.

5
00:00:12,286 --> 00:00:14,616
(Howard:)- Right.
- You also made a grammatical mistake.

6
00:00:14,788 --> 00:00:17,208
You said "nauseous"
when you meant "nauseated."

7
00:00:18,459 --> 00:00:19,879
(Sheldon:)But go on.

8
00:00:20,461 --> 00:00:23,131
(Leonard:)Sheldon, this date
is probably my one chance with Penny.

9
00:00:23,297 --> 00:00:24,627
What happens if I blow it?

10
00:00:25,466 --> 00:00:29,676
(Sheldon:)Well, if we accept your premise and also
accept the highly improbable assumption...

11
00:00:29,845 --> 00:00:32,435
(Sheldon:)...that Penny is the only woman
in the world for you...

12
00:00:32,598 --> 00:00:35,388
(Sheldon:)...we can logically conclude
that the result of blowing it...

13
00:00:35,559 --> 00:00:38,809
(Sheldon:)...would be that you end up a lonely,
bitter old man with no progeny.

14
00:00:38,979 --> 00:00:41,399
(Sheldon:)The image of any number
of evil lighthouse keepers...

15
00:00:41,565 --> 00:00:43,905
...from Scooby-Doo cartoons
comes to mind.

16
00:00:44,526 --> 00:00:45,986
(Leonard:)You're not helping.

17
00:00:46,153 --> 00:00:47,943
All right, what response on my part...

18
00:00:48,113 --> 00:00:50,403
(Sheldon:)...would bring this conversation
to a conclusion?

19
00:00:50,574 --> 00:00:53,164
(Leonard:)Tell me whether or not
to go through with the date.

20
00:00:53,327 --> 00:00:54,747
Schrödinger's cat.

21
00:00:55,662 --> 00:00:58,022
(Leonard:)Wow, that's brilliant.

